 "verdict": "The +-500 window is NOISY as an absolute measure of 'the same reasoning proposition': only 42.9 per cent of the nearest-authority pairs inside it are clearly related. But the noise is not symmetric between codes, and it runs AGAINST the finding rather than for it: beside an Evidence Law citation the nearest authority is related in 9 of 15 cases, beside a Commercial Courts Law citation in 3 of 13. The mechanical measure counts a procedural article as having local co-authority when the nearby fiqh is about the costs claim at the end of the judgment. Correcting for relatedness would WIDEN the Evidence-over-Commercial-Courts gap, not close it, so the reported contrast is a lower bound. The absolute local rates should not be read as rates of connected reasoning."
